[arromdee@crabcake.cs.jhu.edu (Kenneth Arromdee) writes:]
[] I doubt it.  The consensus seems to be that Nethack shouldn't contain
[] non-medieval technology. 
{1st an aside: seems like yo-yos should be okay. what's wrong?}

Why are people worried about nethack staying at medieval technology 
when the game already contains many items that are clearly modern in
origin (like magic markers, pizza, Hawaiian shirts, Keystone Kops,
credit cards, C and K rations, cameras)? Neither yo-yos nor shopping
malls would stray from the current flavor of the game and would only 
add to the fun. If the consensus is that nethack should be stuck 
in a strictly medieval setting, then eliminate the existing non-medieval
elements (like the Tourist class and the above items) and set a precedent 
for furture versions. But personally, I'd rather see the game continue 
along it's current course, medieval spiced with modern odds and ends.
And I'd hate to see the Tourist go.

BTW: Has anyone considered how a shopping mall might affect the Tourist
class? Maybe this could be a way to give him a fighting chance.
Also, I second the water level.

